{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"rebar-debug Phase 2 final local validation:\n\nImplemented bounded criterion-scoped recovery for typed completion token/context exhaustion, a fresh tool-free structured finalizer, fail-closed exact-coverage validation, sanitized multi-attempt telemetry/sidecars, aggregate work limits, and documented behavior. Review-discovered blockers were also closed: PASS comparisons normalize whitespace/casing before contradiction checks; only canonical H2 `Acceptance Criteria` checkboxes are enumerated (never `Plan` checkboxes); bugs without an explicit checklist still receive the independent bug-resolution criterion; and an author-supplied identical bug core is evaluated exactly once without crossing the 32-criterion bound.\n\nRED/GREEN proof: the original held-out recovery oracle was RED on origin/main, then GREEN after the fix. Three defect-seeded mutations independently restored (1) missing recovery dispatch, (2) lowercase/whitespace PASS bypass, (3) global checkbox extraction, and a fourth restored unconditional duplicate bug-core append; each made its hidden oracle RED for the expected assertion, and restoring the implementation returned the hidden suite GREEN. Final hidden result: 5 passed. Refactoring litmus remains contract-level: verdict/error/event shape, exact criteria, execution mode, and persisted diagnostics—not private helpers.\n\nFinal gates: focused recovery/telemetry suite 27 passed; module-size contract 4 passed; `make lint` passed; `make typecheck` passed (380 source files); staged `git diff --check` passed; independent five-axis re-review APPROVED with no blocking findings. Clean full gate: `make test` -> 7,280 passed, 29 skipped, 114 deselected, 13 warnings in 27m19s. An earlier full run also had all 7,272 tests pass but its session isolation backstop correctly rejected my own mid-run staging change; rerunning with the index frozen produced the clean result above. Changed modules remain below the 800-line cap: runner.py 783, gate_dispatch.py 775, completion_recovery.py 539, usage_log.py 206.\n\nFile impact is recorded on the ticket. No external dependency was added, no existing test was weakened, and production callers retain the public validated-verdict-or-typed-error contract. Next: signed Gerrit commit, bot review/Verified gates, Submit, post-merge live reproduction, then close this blocker and resume the dependent completion/epic chain."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785189656560903001,"uuid":"b90b73bb-6f16-4564-a139-5360c06dc907"}